From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 09:51:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip group pre-cal push on MT7992

MT7992 firmware 20260720 corrupts the 2.4 GHz RF state when the
driver applies group pre-cal data from current factory provisioning.
EVM collapses. Rates cap at MCS 2-3 in both directions while RSSI
stays strong and balanced. Firmware 20260310 accepts identical data.

A capped push does not help. Test cap limited the push to the 116772
byte GROUPPREK stream size. This size matches the flash info dword
and the wait threshold in MediaTek mt7996_tm_group_prek().

Skip the group pre-cal push on MT7992 until MediaTek clarifies the
expected provisioning format. Chamber tests on SDG-8713v and
SDG-8712v confirm the workaround. The same firmware reaches
EHT-MCS 13 in both directions with the push skipped.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |   10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -5073,6 +5073,16 @@ int mt7996_mcu_apply_group_cal(struct mt
 	u32 offs = MT_EE_DO_PRE_CAL;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	/* Newer firmware corrupts the MT7992 2.4 GHz RF state when group
+	 * pre-cal data from current factory provisioning is applied.
+	 * Skip the push until MediaTek clarifies the expected
+	 * provisioning format.
+	 */
+	if (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76)) {
+		dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "skipping group pre-cal push\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!cal)
 		return 0;
 
